{"name":"Cistern","hex":"#a9b0b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cistern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A reservoir or tank for holding water, especially for catching and holding rainwater for later use.","In a flush toilet, the container in which the water used for flushing is held; a toilet tank."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cistern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cistern","blocks":[{"text":"A cistern is a waterproof receptacle for holding liquids, usually water. Cisterns are often built to catch and store rainwater. To prevent leakage, the interior of the cistern is often lined with hydraulic plaster."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/El_Jadida_cistern.jpg/330px-El_Jadida_cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cistern"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Well-cistern.jpg/500px-Well-cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Well-cistern.jpg/1280px-Well-cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Well-cistern.jpg/500px-Well-cistern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The difference between a cistern and a well is in the source of the water: A cistern collects fresh water where a well draws from groundwater.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWell-cistern.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Cistern_in_the_Mission_District%2C_San_Francisco%2C_California.jpg/500px-Cistern_in_the_Mission_District%2C_San_Francisco%2C_California.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/